      "body": "## Overview\n\nA NaN value in `logit_bias` is clamped to -100 and silently bans the token, instead of being rejected.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `SamplingParams.from_optional` raises a validation error (`parameter=\"logit_bias\"`) when any bias is NaN.\n- Finite and infinite values behave as before: they are clamped to [-100, 100].\n\n## Validation\n\n`tests/test_sampling_params.py` (2 new tests):\n\n```\npytest tests/test_sampling_params.py\n  main:        2 failed, 62 passed\n  this branch: 64 passed\n```\n\nAlso, on main a JSON body with `\"logit_bias\": {\"5\": NaN}` parsed into `ChatCompletionRequest` gives `to_sampling_params(...).logit_bias == {5: -100.0}`; on this branch it raises `VLLMValidationError`. `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the changed files. I ran the tests on CPU with the xgrammar import stubbed. I did not run a live server, so the HTTP path is checked at the request-model level only. Model evaluation does not apply: no sampling math changes for valid input.\n\n## Details\n\n`min(100.0, max(-100.0, bias))` returns -100.0 for NaN because every comparison with NaN is false. Python's JSON parser accepts the `NaN` literal and pydantic accepts it for `float`, so a request can reach this. The clamp now goes through one helper used by both the fast path and the non-integer-key path in `from_optional`.\n\nNot a duplicate: open PRs and issues searched for `logit_bias` with NaN, non-finite, validation and clamp. #52686 (tests) and #55164 (size limit) do not touch NaN; #46612 (non-integer keys) is merged.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance was used for this change.\n",
